<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= locale %>">
  <head>
    <title><%= [ content_for(:title), site_title ].compact.join(" · ") %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <%= render "shared/theme_head" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind" %>
  </head>

  <%# The plain pages a visitor's form send answers without JavaScript
      CMS-drawn and nothing of the site's theme. Its own small layout and not
      `product`: no CSRF tag (a send carries no token, and this page must
      mint none), no import map and no script of CS Studio, the visitor's
      language, and no CONTENT·SPIEL wordmark linking to the sign-in. The one
      script is the stored light or dark (`shared/theme_head`). The header
      is the site's name, in the visitor's language, as a link back to the
      page the form came from; a site with no name has none, and the page's
      own back link is below. The column is sign-in's, wider (the "simple
      form" width). %>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-paper font-cs text-ink scheme-light dark:scheme-dark">
    <% if site_title %>
      <header class="px-7 py-5">
        <%= link_to site_title, back_path, class: "text-sm font-semibold text-ink" %>
      </header>
    <% end %>
    <main class="px-[22px] pb-16 pt-16">
      <div class="form-send-page mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[560px] flex-col gap-[18px]">
        <%= yield %>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
